{"revision":1,"target":"X86","entries":[{"name":"sim_read","kind":"function","declaration":"long sim_read(long fd, void *buffer, long count)","parameters":[{"label":"long fd","range":[14,21]},{"label":"void *buffer","range":[23,35]},{"label":"long count","range":[37,47]}],"headers":["sim.h"],"summary":"Reads up to count bytes from the file descriptor in fd into the buffer at buffer, and returns how many it read. Descriptor 0 is standard input, so this is how a program reads what was typed. A return of 0 means end of input.","href":"/documentation/x86/syscall#syscall-read","definition":"documentation"},{"name":"sim_write","kind":"function","declaration":"long sim_write(long fd, const void *buffer, long count)","parameters":[{"label":"long fd","range":[15,22]},{"label":"const void *buffer","range":[24,42]},{"label":"long count","range":[44,54]}],"headers":["sim.h"],"summary":"Writes count bytes from the buffer at buffer to the file descriptor in fd, and returns how many it wrote. Descriptor 1 is standard output and 2 is standard error, so this is how a program prints.","href":"/documentation/x86/syscall#syscall-write","definition":"documentation"},{"name":"sim_open","kind":"function","declaration":"long sim_open(const void *path, long flags, long mode)","parameters":[{"label":"const void *path","range":[14,30]},{"label":"long flags","range":[32,42]},{"label":"long mode","range":[44,53]}],"headers":["sim.h"],"summary":"Opens the path at path with the flags in flags and, when creating, the mode in mode. Returns a file descriptor.","href":"/documentation/x86/syscall#syscall-open","definition":"documentation"},{"name":"sim_close","kind":"function","declaration":"long sim_close(long fd)","parameters":[{"label":"long fd","range":[15,22]}],"headers":["sim.h"],"summary":"Closes the file descriptor in fd.","href":"/documentation/x86/syscall#syscall-close","definition":"documentation"},{"name":"sim_stat","kind":"function","declaration":"long sim_stat(const void *path, void *sta